The security and surveillance industry is increasingly adopting artificial intelligence to improve monitoring capabilities, automate video analysis, and identify events in real time. As organizations deploy connected cameras and intelligent monitoring systems, demand is increasing for semiconductor solutions capable of processing visual information efficiently at the device level.

According to Semiconductor Insight, the global AI IPC Chips Market  was valued at USD 170 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 408 million by 2034, growing at a CAGR of 14.7% during the forecast period.

AI IPC chips are integrated circuits designed for intelligent Internet Protocol camera systems. They combine image processing, video encoding, network transmission, and AI acceleration to support functions such as object recognition, scene analysis, and intelligent event detection. By processing data closer to its source, these chips can help reduce dependence on continuous cloud processing for supported applications.

